## Moleculer Services

Moleculer services (`yom-api`, `yom-gateway`, `yom-catalog`, `yom-payments`, `yom-store`, `yom-promotions`, `yom-transactions`, etc.) follow the Moleculer framework conventions and patterns. **Do not apply Hexagonal Architecture or NestJS-specific patterns to these services.**

### Key Characteristics
- Services autodiscover each other via NATS (no manual service registry)
- Actions are defined on service schemas — not controllers
- Inter-service calls use `this.broker.call('service.action', params)`
- `yom-api` uses Express alongside Moleculer for HTTP routing

### When Working on a Moleculer Service
- Follow the existing file and folder structure of the service
- Define actions on the service schema (`actions: { ... }`)
- Use `this.broker.call` for inter-service communication
- Tests use Jest; mock `this.broker` for unit tests
- Do NOT introduce NestJS decorators, modules, or DI patterns into Moleculer services

