## API Design Standards

### REST Endpoints
- Use nouns, not verbs: `/banners` not `/getBanners`
- Plural resource names: `/banners`, `/faqs`, `/customers`
- Nested resources for relationships: `/customers/:id/banners`
- HTTP methods: `GET` (read), `POST` (create), `PUT` (full update), `PATCH` (partial update), `DELETE`

### Response Patterns
- Mutations always return a consistent envelope:
  ```json
  { "message": "Banner created successfully", "data": { } }
  ```
- List endpoints must support pagination:
  ```json
  { "data": [], "metadata": { "total": 100, "page": 1, "limit": 10, "totalPages": 10 } }
  ```

### NestJS Controller Example
```typescript
@Controller('banners')
@UseGuards(AdminGuard)
export class BannerController {
  constructor(private readonly bannerService: BannerService) {}

  @Get()
  async findAll(@Request() req): Promise<BannerResponseDto[]> {
    const { customerId } = req.user;
    return this.bannerService.findAll(customerId);
  }

  @Get(':id')
  async findById(
    @Param('id') id: string,
    @Request() req,
  ): Promise<BannerResponseDto> {
    const { customerId } = req.user;
    return this.bannerService.findById(id, customerId);
  }

  @Post()
  @HttpCode(201)
  async create(
    @Body() dto: CreateBannerDto,
    @Request() req,
  ): Promise<CreateBannerResponseDto> {
    const { customerId } = req.user;
    return this.bannerService.create({ ...dto, customerId });
  }
}
```

